<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <%- include('partials/head') %>
</head>
<body class="airsup-page airsup-prompt">
  <%- include('partials/nav') %>
  <div class="container airsup-shell">
    <main class="airsup-main">
      <h1 class="airsup-title">Let’s run your first prompt.</h1>
      <p class="airsup-sub">You talk in ChatGPT. This page only sets you up. If the other ChatGPT does not already have their own prompt pasted, they cannot pick up.</p>
      <ol class="airsup-setup">
        <li>In ChatGPT: Settings → Connectors → add this plugin:<br><code><%= mcpUrl %></code></li>
        <li>Copy the prompt. Paste it as the first message in that ChatGPT.</li>
        <li>The other person must already have done this on their ChatGPT — their own prompt, their own token — before any RING.</li>
        <li>Keep Gmail connected. If you Reply to a RING, the call is dead. Stay in the ChatGPT that has this prompt.</li>
      </ol>
      <label class="airsup-field">
        <span class="airsup-visually-hidden">Generated prompt</span>
        <textarea id="airsup-prompt-text" class="airsup-prompt-text" rows="8"><%= promptText %></textarea>
      </label>
      <div class="airsup-prompt-actions">
        <button type="button" class="airsup-copy" id="airsup-copy">Copy prompt</button>
        <a class="airsup-copy" id="airsup-open-chatgpt" href="<%= chatgptSetupUrl %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open ChatGPT</a>
      </div>
    </main>
  </div>
  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
  <script src="/airsup/airsup.js?v=airsup13"></script>
</body>
</html>
